<title>UK: N Ireland unemployment lowest since July 1980.</title>
<headline>N Ireland unemployment lowest since July 1980.</headline>
<dateline>BELFAST 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of people unemployed in Northern Ireland fell by a seasonally-adjusted 2,200 in April from the previous month to 64,800, or 8.4 percent, the lowest rate since July 1980, economy minister Baroness Denton said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Denton said in a statement that total unemployment in Northern Ireland was down 21,200 from the same month in 1996.</p>
<p>--Belfast newsroom +44-1232-315-253</p>
